# split — real-world examples

## Split a text file into chunks of 1000 lines

```sh
split -l 1000 access.log
```

## Split a large binary into 10 MB pieces

```sh
split -b 10M bigfile.iso
```

## Use a custom prefix and numeric suffixes

```sh
split -b 100M -d backup.tar.gz backup.part.
```

## Reassemble the pieces

```sh
cat backup.part.* > backup.tar.gz
```

## Split a DB dump so it fits on FAT-formatted media

```sh
split -b 4000M -d homelab-db.sql.gz homelab-db.sql.gz.
```

## Flag reference

| Flag   | What it does                          |
| ------ | ------------------------------------- |
| -l N   | N lines per output file               |
| -b SIZE| SIZE bytes per file (K, M, G suffixes)|
| -d     | numeric suffixes instead of aa, ab…   |
| -a N   | suffix length                         |
